### `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/legal.ts`

Workforce entry point. ~1,100 lines. Key structure:

**`POST /api/v1/legal/matter`** — the single workforce entry point:
```
text → intakeClassify()
     → specialistHandler[matterType]()
     → evaluateGovernance({ output, raw_text, confidence, policy })
     → pool.query(model_usage_events)   // soft-fail
     → return { matter_id, intake, specialist_output, governance_decision, trace, lineage }
```

**Six internal specialist functions:**
- `intakeClassify(text)` → `{ matter_type, confidence, routing_target, reasoning }`
- `contractAnalyze(text)` → `{ risk_flags[], blocking_issues[], next_steps[], overall_risk }`
- `employmentAnalyze(text)` → `{ compliance_flags[], ca_noncompete_void, escalation_required, next_steps[] }`
- `litigationAnalyze(text)` → `{ key_claims[], jurisdiction, recommended_next_steps[], statute_of_limitations_risk }`
- `ipAnalyze(text)` → `{ ip_type, ownership_risk, key_restrictions[], recommended_actions[] }`
- `corporateAnalyze(text)` → `{ governance_clauses[], board_approval_required, compliance_gaps[], next_steps[] }`

**`applyCANoncompeteRule(text, output)`** — post-processing on employment output. Runs before governance. Sets `ca_noncompete_void = true` and `escalation_required = true` if CA non-compete detected. Belt-and-suspenders with governance engine.

